{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15157": {
      "title": "Temporary, Part-Time Interactive and Graphic Design Instructor",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Temporary, Part-Time Interactive and Graphic Design Instructor - (Unsolicited) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Temporary, Part-Time Interactive and Graphic Design Instructor - (Unsolicited) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please Note: Class schedule and modality (face-to-face, online, blended, etc.) is set by the dean of the college. Faculty Posting Details Position Information Requisition Number F02709 Department Art and Design Working Title Temporary, Part-Time Interactive and Graphic Design Instructor - (Unsolicited) Classification Instructor - 24900 Position Summary Information Nature of position Temporary, part-time Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Department of Art & Design needs temporary part-time Instructors for courses in Interactive & Graphic Design, including: Web Design Motion Design Experience Design Package Design Typography Branding Visual Communication Computer Art Temporary, part-time instructor responsible for teaching a variety of topics in Interactive & Graphic Design. In addition, the instructor will write and organize curriculum, prepare lectures and demonstrations, lead discussions, evaluate student performance, grade projects, and submit final grades through MAX . The purpose of this posting is to generate a pool of qualified faculty. Applications submitted will be reviewed on an as needed basis based on enrollment. Anyone meeting the qualifications may be contacted for an interview and potentially hired when a need exists. In the event that you are interviewed but not immediately hired, your application will remain in the departments pool of qualified faculty. A complete application will include: Cover letter describing qualifications for the position. Current curriculum vitae or professional resume. Copies of registrar-issued transcripts for all degrees conferred and in progress. Two letters of professional reference dated within the last 12 months Incomplete applications will not be considered. Applicants are encouraged to submit their application materials far enough in advance of the closing date to allow time for their references to respond. If you choose to provide additional documentation, please upload these items as optional documents. Please do not link your application to the position until you have uploaded all of the required documents and any optional documents you want to provide. You will not be able to change the materials submitted or upload any new additional materials, after the application process has been completed and you receive a confirmation number. Located in Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, Millersville University of Pennsylvania is one of the 10 public universities of Pennsylvania’s State System of Higher Education. Our pillars of distinction include exceptionally strong student-faculty relationships, numerous programs of distinction, a beautiful campus and vibrant location, and successful job placement for our students. Our students’ success, both inside and outside of the classroom, is our highest priority, and we provide numerous opportunities to facilitate their academic, personal, and social growth and development. Almost 70 baccalaureate programs are available for our 6,000 students to find their path.. Approximately one thousand graduate students enroll in 21 master’s and three doctoral programs. Our faculty are highly respected in their fields and dedicated to the success of students in the classroom, research labs, and in campus life. Over 66,000 alumni live in all 50 states and in 72 countries around the world. We seek individuals who embrace and value our EPPIIC values of exploration, public mission, professionalism, inclusion, integrity, and compassion. At Millersville University we are committed to fostering a learning and working environment that promotes diversity to foster a climate of inclusion. EPPIIC values and the principles of Inclusive Excellence are an essential part of the foundation for our learning and working environment. Millersville University is an equal opportunity employer and, in compliance with federal and state laws and university policy, is committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or gender expression. Individuals from traditionally underrepresented populations are encouraged to apply. The State System Employee Benefits Summary for faculty can be found at: https://www.passhe.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefit-summaries/sshe-summary.pdf Duties and Responsibilities Required Qualifications MFA in Graphic Design or equivalent experience. Expertise in Adobe software. Evidence of ability to successfully teach diverse student populations. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal communication skills. Commitment to inclusive practices and working with diverse student populations. Successful interview. Successful teaching demonstration. Successful completion of three background checks. Preferred Qualifications MFA in Graphic Design or related discipline. Prior college-level teaching experience. Prior experience in the design industry. Essential Functions Posting Open Date 03/13/2024 Posting Close Date Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/11522 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts 1 Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Optional Documents Resume Unofficial Transcripts 2 Unofficial Transcripts 3 Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Reference Letter 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15475": {
      "title": "About the position:",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Building Maintenance Foreman - Plumbing Shop Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Building Maintenance Foreman - Plumbing Shop Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is represented by a labor union and is subject to the terms and conditions of the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. This position is designated an essential employee position. Employee is expected to report to work during their designated shift during emergency situations, university closures or delays. Staff Posting Details Position Information Requisition Number P01336 Position Type Staff Department Maintenance Operations Working Title Building Maintenance Foreman - Plumbing Shop Classification Building Maintenance Foreman - 94660 Position Summary Information Nature of position Permanent, Full-time If Temporary, Start Date If Temporary, End Date If part-time, hours per week If part-time, percent time Days Worked Monday to Friday Hours/Shift worked 7:00 a.m. to 3:30 p.m. with occasional overtime. Union AFSCME Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function About the position: Lead and participate in a variety of skilled and semiskilled activities in the installation, maintenance and repair of plumbing fixtures and systems to maintain infrastructure in safe, sanitary, and code compliant working conditions; operate and maintain the campus potable water, sanitary, and storm sewer infrastructure; develop and implement plumbing projects; and manage assigned personnel. Join Our Team at Millersville University! Salary Range: $56,541.00 – $59,003.00 annually Plus a generous benefits package designed to support your well-being and future: Comprehensive Health Coverage – Medical, dental, and vision insurance Group Life Insurance Retirement Plans – Choose from two excellent options Tuition Waiver – Invest in your education or your family’s Paid Time Off – Vacation, sick leave, and holidays to recharge Full Benefits Summary ( PDF ) Why Millersville? Nestled in beautiful Lancaster County, Pennsylvania , Millersville University is a proud member of Pennsylvania’s State System of Higher Education. We’re known for: Strong student-faculty connections 70+ undergraduate and 24 graduate programs A stunning campus and vibrant community Outstanding job placement for graduates With over 66,000 alumni across the globe, our impact is far-reaching—and growing. Our Mission & Values: At Millersville, we live by our EPPIIC values of Exploration, Public Mission, Professionalism, Inclusion, Integrity, and Compassion. We are deeply committed to Inclusive Excellence —creating a welcoming, supportive environment where everyone can thrive. We believe diversity is a strength, and we actively seek individuals who bring unique perspectives and experiences to our community. Equal Opportunity for All: Millersville University is an equal opportunity employer . We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination. Individuals from traditionally underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged to apply . Duties and Responsibilities Lead and participate in a variety of skilled and semi-skilled activities in the planning, estimating, and scheduling work installation, maintenance and repair of plumbing fixtures and systems. Ensure compliance with building, health and safety laws, codes, regulations, and standards applicable to the plumbing trade. Supervise, train, and provide work direction and guidance to assigned personnel; assign employee duties, inspect, and evaluate work for quality and safety; review work for accuracy, completeness and compliance with established standards and procedures; oversee operation and scheduling of the plumbing shop. Work on systems including but not limited to domestic water, heating/chilled water, fire protection, waste, stormwater, air, vent, steam, and gas infrastructure/piping. Work on hot water heaters, boilers, heat exchangers, grease traps, oil water separators, sump pumps, lint interceptors, and other equipment. Manage the water production, treatment, storage, and distribution of potable water for the campus. Develop and implement plumbing installation, maintenance, repair, and enhancement projects; estimate labor, material, and equipment requirements for projects; monitor, assess and modify activities in response to project progress. Mange the repair, maintenance, and replacement of kitchen equipment. Coordinate contracted welding services and maintenance plumbing work; inspect contract work; and authorize payments. Coordinate work and communicate progress with building occupants and others as needed. Maintain accurate and complete documentation to include labor time, materials, equipment, and contract support for completed work in department’s work order system. Exercise independent judgment in the performance of their trade and work from oral or written instructions, sketches, and blueprints; make sound decisions for minor projects that have no detailed drawings or conflicting information; trouble shoot systems/components to identify issue and resolve issue. Manage the annual operating budget; forecast major expenses and recapitalization of equipment; and restock materials and equipment. Safety and efficiently operate hand and power tools and equipment common to the trade; and drive a state vehicle and other equipment in the performance of work. Manage assigned personnel to include employee interviews, performance evaluations, union relationships, conflicts, disciplinary actions, safety, and in-service training as needed. Will be contacted about and respond to issues after designated shift. Response may require onsite presence to resolve issue or recalling appropriate personnel (employees or contractors) to assist with the problem. Professionally and thoroughly address customer complaints. Other duties as assigned. SAFETY : Investigate accidents and incidents. Initiates appropriate action to mitigate issues. Prepares written reports. Work safely by using Personal Protective Equipment, maintaining equipment, following safety procedures and policies, etc. Ensure staff follows same process. Conduct safety training for direct reports within first two weeks of start date and monthly thereafter. Ensure personnel have required training and certification to perform their duties. Take appropriate supervisory action if safety standards are not being followed. Maintain SDS for chemicals related to the department. Be aware of and report potential safety hazards immediately. Resolve pending hazards in a timely fashion. Consult with supervisor or Environmental Health & Safety staff as needed to resolve unsafe conditions or obtain additional training/resources. Stop unsafe practice regardless of shop or contractor if actions could imminently endanger life or result in significant property damage. Required Qualifications Two years of experience at the journey level divided among a minimum two of the building, electrical, or mechanical trades; and such training as may have been gained through graduation from high school or vocational school; OR any equivalent combination of experience and training. Possess or obtain within first 12 months of employment the PA DEP Water Plant Operator license. Maintain compliance with program requirements and license while employed in this University position. (Certification cost covered by employer) Possess a wide range of knowledge concerning the use, application, and care of a wide range of hand tools and power tools. Demonstrated knowledge of: standard practices and tools of multiple trades. occupational hazards and safety precautions. Demonstrated ability to be proactive, predict needs and implement change. Ability to: plan, assign, supervise and evaluate work. train and instruct staff on safety precautions. work independently and with others prepare/maintain appropriate records/reports. make and work from sketches or plans for improvement or alterations of buildings, grounds, and equipment. make accurate estimates of time and materials required for repair and maintenance work. Work experience enforcing procedures regulated by federal, state, or local governments. Ability to work with individuals from diverse cultures, racial, religious, and ethnic groups. Demonstrated strong analytical and excellent problem-solving skills. Attention to detail. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal communication skills. Commitment to inclusive practices and working with diverse student populations. Successful interview. Successful completion of three background checks. Preferred Qualifications Supervisory experience within the building maintenance field. Prior work experience in a union environment. Prior work experience in a university environment. Essential Functions Please Note: These duties are to be performed with or without an accommodation. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations in accordance with Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ). Individuals must be able to work in all kinds of climates. Work is both indoors and outdoors. Work may be in confined or otherwise restricted environments (such as in an excavated trench/hole). Work environment may be hot, cold, dry, wet, humid, and/or noisy from other construction activities or operation of building equipment. Individual will encounter dust, odors, debris, chemicals, mold, ACM , lead based paint and other potentially hazardous materials. May have to work in cramped spaces or otherwise uncomfortable positions in the performance of assigned tasks. Must be able to wear Personal Protective Equipment, when necessary, hard hats, respirators, eye protection, hearing protection, etc. Physical dexterity in limbs and digits to operate hand and power-driven tools and equipment commonly used in the plumbing field to include frequent computer work. Physical ability to lift, carry, push, and/or pull up to 50 pounds on a regular basis, and occasionally up to 100 pounds. Ability to: continually walk, stand, climb, stoop, bend, kneel, crawl, squat, reach in all directions and have full range of motion of arms, shoulders, back, hips and legs. maintain balance working off the ground using ladders, scaffolds, and/or mechanical lifts. to work in person on campus. climb ladders and work in high, precarious places. sit and/or stand for extended periods of time. see and read with or without vision aids. climb stairs. hear, speak and write/type to exchange information with department personnel and campus community. see to perform maintenance duties and read blueprints, drawings, and specifications. Power grasping and hand/wrist twisting. Advanced math skills (fractions, percentages, formulas, and equations) Extensive writing skills (prepare and organize complex documents). Possess and maintain a valid driver’s license. Posting Open Date 08/12/2026 Posting Close Date 09/09/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants This position is represented by a labor union and is subject to the terms and conditions of the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. This position is designated an essential employee position. Employee is expected to report to work during their designated shift during emergency situations, university closures or delays. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15358 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts 1 Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Reference Letter 3 DD 214 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/14447": {
      "title": "Instructor of MS Integrated Scientific Applications",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Instructor of MS Integrated Scientific Applications - (Unsolicited) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Instructor of MS Integrated Scientific Applications - (Unsolicited) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Faculty Posting Details Position Information Requisition Number F02655 Department Earth Sciences Working Title Instructor of MS Integrated Scientific Applications - (Unsolicited) Classification Instructor - 24900 Position Summary Information Nature of position Temporary, part-time Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Department of Earth Sciences is accepting applications for temporary part-time instructors to teach graduate courses in an accelerated 7 week online asynchronous format . The Earth Science Department at times needs temporary part-time Instructors to fill in for faculty on sabbaticals or leaves. The purpose of this posting is to generate a pool of qualified faculty. Applications submitted will be reviewed on an as needed basis based on enrollment. Anyone meeting the qualifications may be contacted for an interview and potentially hired when a need exists. In the event that you are interviewed but not immediately hired, your application will remain in the departments pool of qualified faculty. A complete application will include: Cover letter describing qualifications for the position. Current curriculum vitae or professional resume. Copies of registrar-issued transcripts for all degrees conferred and in progress. Two letters of professional reference dated within the last 12 months. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Applicants are encouraged to submit their application materials far enough in advance of the closing date to allow time for their references to respond. If you choose to provide additional documentation, please upload these items as optional documents. Please do not link your application to the position until you have uploaded all of the required documents and any optional documents you want to provide. You will not be able to change the materials submitted or upload any new additional materials, after the application process has been completed and you receive a confirmation number. Located in Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, Millersville University of Pennsylvania is one of the 10 public universities of Pennsylvania’s State System of Higher Education. Our pillars of distinction include exceptionally strong student-faculty relationships, numerous programs of distinction, a beautiful campus and vibrant location, and successful job placement for our students. Our students’ success, both inside and outside of the classroom, is our highest priority, and we provide numerous opportunities to facilitate their academic, personal, and social growth and development. Almost 70 baccalaureate programs are available for our 6,000 students to find their path. Approximately one thousand graduate students enroll in 21 master’s and three doctoral programs. Our faculty are highly respected in their fields and dedicated to the success of students in the classroom, research labs, and in campus life. Over 66,000 alumni live in all 50 states and in 72 countries around the world. We seek individuals who embrace and value our EPPIIC values of exploration, public mission, professionalism, inclusion, integrity, and compassion. At Millersville University we are committed to fostering a learning and working environment that promotes diversity to foster a climate of inclusion. EPPIIC values and the principles of Inclusive Excellence are an essential part of the foundation for our learning and working environment. Millersville University is an equal opportunity employer and, in compliance with federal and state laws and university policy, is committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or gender expression. Individuals from traditionally underrepresented populations are encouraged to apply. The State System Employee Benefits Summary for faculty can be found at: https://www.passhe.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefit-summaries/sshe-summary.pdf Duties and Responsibilities Required Qualifications Master’s Degree in field relevant to the area of application or related discipline Evidence of ability to successfully teach diverse student populations. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal communication skills. Commitment to inclusive practices and working with diverse student populations. Successful interview. Successful teaching demonstration for class teaching assignments in an online asynchronous environment. Successful completion of three background checks. Preferred Qualifications PhD or ABD in field relevant to area of application or related discipline. Professional experience in the business or non-profit industries. Demonstrated experience teaching in an online asynchronous environment. Prior college-level teaching experience. Essential Functions Posting Open Date 08/09/2023 Posting Close Date Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/10888 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts 1 Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Optional Documents Resume Unofficial Transcripts 2 Unofficial Transcripts 3 Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Reference Letter 3 Other Document 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
