    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15431": {
      "title": "About the position:",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Cook 1 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Cook 1 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is represented by a labor union and is subject to the terms and conditions of the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. The ability to work on campus. Flexible work schedule as dictated by the needs of the university. Dining and Conference Services staff may be required to work evenings and weekends. This position is designated an essential employee position. Employee is expected to report to work during their designated shift during emergency situations, university closures or delays. Staff Posting Details Position Information Requisition Number P01325 Position Type Staff Department Dining and Catering Services Working Title Cook 1 Classification Cook 1 - 81150 Position Summary Information Nature of position Permanent, Full-time If Temporary, Start Date If Temporary, End Date If part-time, hours per week If part-time, percent time Days Worked varies Hours/Shift worked varies Union AFSCME Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function About the position: Cook, grill, bake, steam, sauté, and fry food for student meals, catering, conferences. Responsible for sanitation of work area and equipment. Join Our Team at Millersville University! Hourly Rate: $18.83 Plus a generous benefits package designed to support your well-being and future: Comprehensive Health Coverage – Medical, dental, and vision insurance Group Life Insurance Retirement Plans – Choose from two excellent options Tuition Waiver – Invest in your education or your family’s Paid Time Off – Vacation, sick leave, and holidays to recharge Full Benefits Summary( PDF ) Why Millersville? Nestled in beautiful Lancaster County, Pennsylvania , Millersville University is a proud member of Pennsylvania’s State System of Higher Education. We’re known for: Strong student-faculty connections 70+ undergraduate and 24 graduate programs A stunning campus and vibrant community Outstanding job placement for graduates With over 66,000 alumni across the globe, our impact is far-reaching—and growing. Our Mission & Values: At Millersville, we live by our EPPIIC values of Exploration, Public Mission, Professionalism, Inclusion, Integrity, and Compassion. We are deeply committed to Inclusive Excellence —creating a welcoming, supportive environment where everyone can thrive. We believe diversity is a strength, and we actively seek individuals who bring unique perspectives and experiences to our community. Equal Opportunity for All: Millersville University is an equal opportunity employer . We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination. Individuals from traditionally underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged to apply . Duties and Responsibilities Mixing, chopping, dicing, grating, slicing, assembling food in preparation for cooking, baking, or assembling, grilling, baking, steaming, or frying foods. Prepare meats for cooking: Skinning, boning, trimming, stuffing, etc., as well as cooking the final product. Prepares menu items for student meals in Gordinier and Lyle Dining Halls and catering functions in-house and off-campus. Maintain records for the Service Summary Reports. Cleaning and sanitation of utensils, equipment, and facilities. May function as lead worker by coordinating, participating in and reviewing routine food production tasks performed by food service workers or student workers. Can train food service workers or student workers in routine food production tasks. Prepare requisitions for cooking ingredients and supplies Maintain recipe files. Check attendance for staff in the area. All other duties as assigned. SAFETY Work safely by using Personal Protective Equipment, maintaining equipment, following safety procedures and policies, etc. Leave the work area clean and functional at the end of shift Be aware of and report any potential safety hazards to supervisor or management immediately Cooperate with safety investigations and audits Attend safety training sessions and maintain licenses, certifications, etc. Required Qualifications One year experience in cooking or quantity commercial or institutional food production or equivalent combination of experience and/or training. Demonstrated knowledge of cooking ingredients, food production safety & sanitation. Experience: Preparing ingredients and cooking food items on a quantity basis. Reading and interpreting recipes Performing recipe extensions. Operating modern kitchen equipment. Garnishing and presenting food for buffets and student dining. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal communication skills. Commitment to inclusive practices and working with diverse student populations. Successful interview. Successful completion of three background checks. Preferred Qualifications Associate degree from a qualified Culinary or Food Service Institution. Experience as a restaurant cook. Essential Functions Please Note: These duties are to be performed with or without an accommodation. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations in accordance with Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ). Ability to: Lift up to 40 lbs. without assistance. Lift over 40 lbs. with assistance. Work in a high heat environment due to heat producing kitchen equipment. Work in cold storage areas. Basic math skills (add, subtract, multiply, divide). Read ingredient lists, recipes, cooking techniques, cooking instructions, service directions and labels. Properly handle and safely use kitchen knives Work as a member of a culinary team. Understanding of written directions Understanding of verbal directions. Familiarity with cooking terminology, cooking equipment, knife handling & cutting skills, sanitation, and kitchen safety. Dexterity of hands and fingers to operate a computer keyboard and mouse. Posting Open Date 07/22/2026 Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants This position is represented by a labor union and is subject to the terms and conditions of the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. The ability to work on campus. Flexible work schedule as dictated by the needs of the university. Dining and Conference Services staff may be required to work evenings and weekends. This position is designated an essential employee position. Employee is expected to report to work during their designated shift during emergency situations, university closures or delays. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15240 Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts 1 Unofficial Transcripts 2 Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Reference Letter 3 DD 214 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
